    "\r",
    "If someone calls `Object.create(null)` and then adds the expected properties, `hasOwnProperty` will not be available on the object itself. \r",
    "\r",
    "fixes algolia/react-instantsearch#2568\r",
    "\r",
    "* fix(ssr): avoid duplicate serializing (algolia/react-instantsearch#2726)\r",
    "\r",
    "* fix(ssr): avoid duplicate serializing\r",
    "\r",
    "Response of `findResultsState` (and `resultsState` prop) before:\r",
    "\r",
    "```js\r",
    "const resultsState = {\r",
    "  content: SearchResults(state: searchParameters, results: rawResults),\r",
    "  state: searchParameters,\r",
    "  _originalResponse: {\r",
    "    results: rawResults\r",
    "  },\r",
    "};\r",
    "```\r",
    "\r",
    "Note that `SearchResults` has the properties `_rawResults` & `_state`. This means that when we serialize, we are retrieving the original response and state twice.\r",
    "\r",
    "Then on further searching, I also find that we don't need to serialize the `SearchResults` object at all, since only the raw response and state is used.\r",
    "\r",
    "I modified this to be more consistent and no longer have duplication:\r",
    "\r",
    "```js\r",
    "const resultsState = {\r",
    "  state: searchParameters,\r",
    "  rawResults,\r",
    "};\r",
    "```\r",
    "\r",
    "The `SearchParameters` object gets serialized without issue, as before.\r",
    "\r",
    "This change in shape has of course also an impact on the shape of `resultsState`, the prop, but that is fine, since it was previously typed as `any`.\r",
    "\r",
    "To be able to type it correctly, I had to add `@types/algoliasearch` & update `algoliasearch-helper` for typescript though.\r",
    "\r",
    "This was initially noticed by @cloakedninjas, thanks!\r",
